<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:cf="using:Cornflower.Controls"
                    xmlns:wp81="using:Cornflower.Themes.Wp81">
  <!--
    The Windows Phone 8.1 AutoSuggestBox, as a theme for Avalonia's AutoCompleteBox: the default style of the 8.1 Update 1
    runtime (autosuggestbox.json, which equals the SDK's generic.xaml), re-expressed, every value by the phone's resource
    key through DynamicResource. docs/controls/AutoSuggestBox/PLAN.md has the values, their sources and every API
    difference.

    The template is the phone's, part for part:
    - PART_TextBox is the phone's TextBox part: Wp81's TextBox (#36), keyed by type, as the phone's takes its default
      style, with no margin of its own; the control's own margin is TextControlMarginThemeThickness, as the phone's. The
      header is cf:ControlHeader.Header and HeaderTemplate (WinRT's Header), passed on to the box's.
    - PART_Popup is the phone's SuggestionsPopup: drawn in the window's overlay layer, as the phone has one window, and
      hung from the box's bottom border (PhoneSuggestionList moves it up by the border, so the two borders lie on each
      other, and gives it the room down to the keyboard).
    - SuggestionsContainer, the box's width, white (AutoSuggestBackgroundThemeBrush, the same in both themes) in a 2.5
      border of the accent (PhoneAccentBrush, TextControlBorderThemeThickness).
    - PART_SelectingItemsControl is the phone's SuggestionsList, a ListView: Wp81's ListBox, its items the phone's
      ListViewItems in the AutoSuggestBox's ItemContainerStyle (AutoSuggestListViewItemMargin, ContentControlFontSize,
      TextBoxForegroundThemeBrush, so the text is black on the white list in both themes).

    What the phone's control does that Avalonia's doesn't by default, set here:
    - FilterMode None: the phone's control doesn't filter; the app gives the suggestions as ItemsSource.
    - MinimumPrefixLength 0: the phone tells the app of every change the user makes, to nothing too.
    - MinimumPopulateDelay 150 ms: the phone raises TextChanged (UserInput), the app's cue, 150 to 177 ms after the key
      (#150); Avalonia's cue is Populating, and the list opens after it, so the list comes when the phone's does. It is
      Avalonia's wait after the last key: a key within 150 ms of the one before starts it again (the phone's two quick
      keys weren't read).
    - PhoneSuggestionList (internal): the list's place and height, and Back and the keyboard closing it.

    The phone's Orientation states change nothing. FocusAdorner is cleared: the box's Focused state is the focus look.
  -->

  <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type AutoCompleteBox}" TargetType="AutoCompleteBox">
    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="{DynamicResource TextControlMarginThemeThickness}" />
    <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Top" />
    <Setter Property="FilterMode" Value="None" />
    <Setter Property="MinimumPrefixLength" Value="0" />
    <Setter Property="MinimumPopulateDelay" Value="0:0:0.15" />
    <!-- The TextBox part's placeholder brush, which the template passes on (Avalonia's AutoCompleteBox has its own). -->
    <Setter Property="PlaceholderForeground" Value="{DynamicResource TextBoxPlaceholderTextThemeBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="FocusAdorner" Value="{x:Null}" />
    <Setter Property="wp81:PhoneSuggestionList.IsEnabled" Value="True" />
    <Setter Property="Template">
      <ControlTemplate>
        <Grid>
          <TextBox x:Name="PART_TextBox"
                   Margin="0"
                   cf:ControlHeader.Header="{TemplateBinding (cf:ControlHeader.Header)}"
                   cf:ControlHeader.HeaderTemplate="{TemplateBinding (cf:ControlHeader.HeaderTemplate)}"
                   CaretIndex="{TemplateBinding CaretIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"
                   ClearSelectionOnLostFocus="{TemplateBinding ClearSelectionOnLostFocus}"
                   DataValidationErrors.Errors="{TemplateBinding (DataValidationErrors.Errors)}"
                   PlaceholderText="{TemplateBinding PlaceholderText}"
                   PlaceholderForeground="{TemplateBinding PlaceholderForeground}"
                   MaxLength="{TemplateBinding MaxLength}"
                   InnerLeftContent="{TemplateBinding InnerLeftContent}"
                   InnerRightContent="{TemplateBinding InnerRightContent}" />
          <!-- The placement no positioner adjusts: PhoneSuggestionList gives the list the room it has below the box. A tap
               elsewhere closes the list (Avalonia's light dismiss); a tap on the box goes to the box, the list staying. -->
          <Popup x:Name="PART_Popup"
                 PlacementTarget="{Binding #PART_TextBox}"
                 Placement="Bottom"
                 PlacementConstraintAdjustment="None"
                 ShouldUseOverlayLayer="True"
                 IsLightDismissEnabled="True"
                 OverlayInputPassThroughElement="{Binding #PART_TextBox}">
            <Border x:Name="SuggestionsContainer"
                    Width="{Binding #PART_TextBox.Bounds.Width}"
                    Background="{DynamicResource AutoSuggestBackgroundThemeBrush}"
                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource PhoneAccentBrush}"
                    BorderThickness="{DynamicResource TextControlBorderThemeThickness}">
              <ListBox x:Name="PART_SelectingItemsControl"
                       Focusable="False"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource TextBoxForegroundThemeBrush}"
                       ItemTemplate="{TemplateBinding ItemTemplate}"
                       ScrollViewer.IsScrollChainingEnabled="False">
                <!-- The phone's ItemContainerStyle: the list's own items, over the ListViewItem theme's values. Neither the
                     list nor its items take the focus, so a tap on a suggestion leaves it in the box and the keyboard up,
                     as on the phone; the box's own keys move through the list (Avalonia's selection adapter). -->
                <ListBox.Styles>
                  <Style Selector="ListBox#PART_SelectingItemsControl > ListBoxItem">
                    <Setter Property="Focusable" Value="False" />
                    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="{DynamicResource AutoSuggestListViewItemMargin}" />
                    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource ContentControlFontSize}" />
                    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextBoxForegroundThemeBrush}" />
                  </Style>
                </ListBox.Styles>
              </ListBox>
            </Border>
          </Popup>
        </Grid>
      </ControlTemplate>
    </Setter>
  </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
